NNAAMMEE
       blkdiscard - discard sectors on a device

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       bbllkkddiissccaarrdd [options] [--oo _o_f_f_s_e_t] [--ll _l_e_n_g_t_h] _d_e_v_i_c_e

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       bbllkkddiissccaarrdd is used to discard device sectors. This is useful for
       solid-state drivers (SSDs) and thinly-provisioned storage. Unlike
       ffssttrriimm(8), this command is used directly on the block device.

       By default, bbllkkddiissccaarrdd will discard all blocks on the device. Options
       may be used to modify this behavior based on range or size, as
       explained below.

       The _d_e_v_i_c_e argument is the pathname of the block device.

       WWAARRNNIINNGG:: AAllll ddaattaa iinn tthhee ddiissccaarrddeedd rreeggiioonn oonn tthhee ddeevviiccee wwiillll bbee lloosstt!!

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       The _o_f_f_s_e_t and _l_e_n_g_t_h arguments may be followed by the multiplicative
       suffixes KiB (=1024), MiB (=1024*1024), and so on for GiB, TiB, PiB,
       EiB, ZiB and YiB (the "iB" is optional, e.g., "K" has the same meaning
       as "KiB") or the suffixes KB (=1000), MB (=1000*1000), and so on for
       GB, TB, PB, EB, ZB and YB.

       --ff, ----ffoorrccee
           Disable all checking. Since v2.36 the block device is open in
           exclusive mode (OO__EEXXCCLL) by default to avoid collision with mounted
           filesystem or another kernel subsystem. The ----ffoorrccee option disables
           the exclusive access mode.

       --oo, ----ooffffsseett _o_f_f_s_e_t
           Byte offset into the device from which to start discarding. The
           provided value must be aligned to the device sector size. The
           default value is zero.

       --ll, ----lleennggtthh _l_e_n_g_t_h
           The number of bytes to discard (counting from the starting point).
           The provided value must be aligned to the device sector size. If
           the specified value extends past the end of the device, bbllkkddiissccaarrdd
           will stop at the device size boundary. The default value extends to
           the end of the device.

       --pp, ----sstteepp _l_e_n_g_t_h
           The number of bytes to discard within one iteration. The default is
           to discard all by one ioctl call.

       --ss, ----sseeccuurree
           Perform a secure discard. A secure discard is the same as a regular
           discard except that all copies of the discarded blocks that were
           possibly created by garbage collection must also be erased. This
           requires support from the device.

       --zz, ----zzeerroooouutt
           Zero-fill rather than discard.

       --vv, ----vveerrbboossee
           Display the aligned values of _o_f_f_s_e_t and _l_e_n_g_t_h. If the ----sstteepp
           option is specified, it prints the discard progress every second.

       --hh, ----hheellpp
           Display help text and exit.

       --VV, ----vveerrssiioonn
           Print version and exit.

